{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890064",
      "title": "Grouping Tests Together With Test Suites",
      "sourceHash": "0e3f9a090621a96a3b860e647de2944e4a7bdb89cf2c0dccf8b8de99a9a279b2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 5.34,
          "en": "Now with our first custom tests written,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.34,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "before we write more tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 11.653,
          "en": "let's talk about this tests suites vs. tests thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 14.46,
          "en": "As your application grows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.46,
          "end": 16.12,
          "en": "you typically will have dozens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.12,
          "end": 19.54,
          "en": "or maybe hundreds or thousands of tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.54,
          "end": 23.15,
          "en": "and to organize and group those different tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.15,
          "end": 27.3,
          "en": "you often organize them into different testing suites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.3,
          "end": 31.21,
          "en": "For example, all the tests, belonging to one feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.21,
          "end": 33.83,
          "en": "or one component of your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.83,
          "end": 36.123,
          "en": "could be grouped into one testing suite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.3,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "and you create such a testing suite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 44.15,
          "en": "by using the global \"describe\" function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.15,
          "end": 48.383,
          "en": "Just like \"test,\" that's a globally available function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.24,
          "end": 51.56,
          "en": "You also give these two arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.56,
          "end": 54.41,
          "en": "where the first argument is a description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.41,
          "end": 57.32,
          "en": "and this is a description of this category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.32,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "to which your different tests will then belong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 64.73,
          "en": "and here it could be \"Greeting,\" like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.73,
          "end": 67.66,
          "en": "or \"Greeting component\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.66,
          "end": 70.21000000000001,
          "en": "to make it clear that we're talking about the tests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.21000000000001,
          "end": 72.787,
          "en": "belonging to the \"Greeting component.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 75.76,
          "en": "Then you have a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.76,
          "end": 79.1,
          "en": "which also is an anonymous function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.1,
          "end": 80.16,
          "en": "But in this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.16,
          "end": 83.26,
          "en": "you don't write the testing code itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.26,
          "end": 86.69,
          "en": "but you put your different tests in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.69,
          "end": 91.09,
          "en": "So we kept this test and added in this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.09,
          "end": 92.71000000000001,
          "en": "And now we've got one suite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.71000000000001,
          "end": 94.15,
          "en": "with one test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.15,
          "end": 95.95,
          "en": "and we can have multiple suites",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.95,
          "end": 98.503,
          "en": "and we can also have multiple tests per suite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 102.33,
          "en": "So if I now saved this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.33,
          "end": 105.27000000000001,
          "en": "you see that we still have this description text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.27000000000001,
          "end": 109.12,
          "en": "but it's grouped below this testing group name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.12,
          "end": 111.4,
          "en": "this testing suite name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.4,
          "end": 113.81,
          "en": "and you see that we have one testing suite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.81,
          "end": 116.12,
          "en": "and one test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.12,
          "end": 117.55,
          "en": "The same as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.55,
          "end": 120.67,
          "en": "because if we have no explicitly set suite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.67,
          "end": 122.27,
          "en": "we get one automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.27,
          "end": 126.31,
          "en": "But now, we do have our own clearly labeled suite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.31,
          "end": 127.55,
          "en": "which is a good idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.55,
          "end": 129.25,
          "en": "As your application grows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.25,
          "end": 132.423,
          "en": "you definitely want to group your tests like this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}